AmiPixelShop 0.7.1 - Early Beta
===============================

A modern, layer-based image editor written natively for the Amiga.
Not a port and nothing reverse-engineered: written from scratch in plain
C and 68k assembler, running on its own RTG screen up to 1920x1080.

Source code, bug reports and the latest version:

    https://github.com/radi7777/AmiPixelShop

TESTERS WANTED! There are certainly still many bugs. Please report them
on GitHub (Issues). Read Guide.html in the archive for instructions
(works in IBrowse, AWeb and Voyager).

Features
--------
- AI: Generative Fill with a text prompt, Remove (button or brush),
  Extend (outpainting), Select Subject, Remove Background - directly
  from the Amiga via OpenRouter (needs AmiSSL v5 and an API key)
- Layers (up to 64), 25 blend modes, opacity/fill, locks, groups
- Layer masks, group masks, clipping masks, adjustment layers
- Layer styles: drop shadow, outer glow, stroke
- Brush, eraser, clone stamp, history brush, spot healing, blur/sharpen/
  smudge, dodge/burn, gradient, paint bucket, shapes
- Marquee, lasso, magnetic lasso, quick selection, magic wand, color range,
  grow, similar, border, smooth
- Editable TrueType text (stays editable when rotated or transformed),
  pen tool with Bezier paths
- Free transform, crop, image/canvas size, image rotation
- Filters: gaussian/box/motion blur, unsharp mask, median, noise, emboss,
  find edges, high pass, mosaic
- Levels with histogram, Auto and per-channel R/G/B, Curves with histogram
- Undo/redo with history panel, multiple documents
- Rulers and guides; selections, shapes, crop and the move tool snap
  to guides, image edges and layer edges
- Built-in update: checks GitHub at start (when online), installs
  new versions and restarts (can be turned off in the Help menu)
- Reduce Colors: optimized palettes (24 bit, OCS 12 bit, MagicWB),
  2-256 colors, EHB, HAM6, HAM8, dithering, live preview
- New Document presets for the classic Amiga screen modes
- Native .aps format, layered PSD import, IFF ILBM import and export,
  PNG, JPEG, datatypes

Requirements
------------
- PiStorm with Emu68 (JIT-emulated 68040 + FPU) - recommended
- maybe a real 68060 with FPU and RTG (untested)
- AmigaOS 3.2, Picasso96/P96 with a 24 or 32 bit screen mode
  (without Picasso96: CyberGraphX, e.g. MorphOS - untested)
- 128 MB Fast RAM or more
- for the AI features: Roadshow, AmiSSL v5, OpenRouter API key

Tested on an Amiga 500 with PiStorm (Pi 3A+, Emu68) and AmigaOS 3.2.3.

Installation
------------
Unpack the archive anywhere and start AmiPixelShop. On the first start
choose a screen mode. For the Type tool put TrueType fonts into
FONTS:truetype/.

License
-------
MIT License. Uses stb (Public Domain/MIT), zlib (zlib License) and the
Open Sans font (Apache License 2.0).

Developed by a professional art designer with the help of Claude.

Note on the uploader address: it is written without the @ and the dot
to keep address harvesters out. Put an @ before "gmail" and a dot in
front of "com" and you have it.


AmiPixelShop - Ebenen-Bildbearbeitung fuer den Amiga
====================================================

Eine moderne Bildbearbeitung mit Ebenen, nativ fuer den Amiga
geschrieben: kein Port, nichts nachgebaut per Reverse Engineering,
sondern von Grund auf in C und 68k-Assembler. Laeuft auf einem eigenen
RTG-Bildschirm bis 1920x1080.

Fruehe Beta - Tester gesucht! Fehler bitte auf GitHub melden:

    https://github.com/radi7777/AmiPixelShop

Voraussetzungen: PiStorm (Emu68) oder evtl. 68060 mit FPU, AmigaOS 3.2,
RTG mit 24/32 Bit, mindestens 128 MB RAM. Anleitung: Guide.html im
Archiv (IBrowse, AWeb, Voyager).

Hinweis zur Uploader-Adresse: sie steht ohne @ und ohne Punkt da, damit
Adresssammler nichts davon haben. Ein @ vor "gmail", ein Punkt vor
"com", fertig.
